  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "Ul0W0E/mNR9c9k/yDdoYSwxHstE=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-19T11:30:10.858Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "PPI AG brings 40+ years in banking and insurance and is described as the payments market leader, which is genuine depth in exactly the vertical the payments and claims hypotheses target. The problem is what that depth rests on: it owns its payments product IP.\n\nOwning product IP is the recurring disqualifier across this set. A firm whose revenue depends on its own payments products has that product sitting in the application-layer slot an engagement would need, so the relationship is structurally competitive even where the technical fit looks strong.\n\nIts stack was not otherwise researched. It sits at priority 4 needing an open-source screen, but the constraint here is the product ownership, which a posture screen would not address.\n\n---\n\n## Leads sharing this finding (1)\n\n**4 \u00b7 needs OSS screen**\n- PPI AG (DE)\n\nVerbatim research text this claim was extracted from:\n\n> 40+ years banking/insurance, payments market leader. Deep but owns product IP.",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-19T11:30:10.858692Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-19T11:30:10.858696Z"
    }
  },
